    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33563" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pammĕnes</span></b> , is,
		m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				Greek rhetorician</i>, <i>instructor of
			Brutus</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Brut. 97, 332</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Or. 30,
				105</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Att. 5, 20, 2</span></i>.—Hence,
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pammĕnia</span></b> ,
				ōrum, n., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Pammenes</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pammenia illa mihi non placent,</span>”
				<i>those views of Pammenes</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 6, 2, 10</span></i>
			.</div>
